			<div class="content" id="post-content-2272951">
									

<p>Euclid SCPs are usually defined by unpredictability and inability to &quot;just lock it up and expect nothing to happen&quot;. Once someone sees it, its anomalous effect is invoked. Granted that it can follow the subject who observed it, containment breach is a rather real concern in containing this SCP.</p>
<p>Object Classes are not really based on what an SCP does. It's more of &quot;How do I lock it away and make normal society don't know about it?&quot; (As far as my head-canon of Object Classes are concerned)</p>

